<p id="S3.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">For any real number <math id="S3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and positive integers <math id="S3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 7</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, we will show that</span></p>
