<div id="S3.Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.5</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any positive integer <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

